### Create a ticket in the seeded "Sprint 1" (needs EXERCISE D to actually succeed)
# This single request only proves the generator works once - it does NOT exercise
# concurrency; that is only covered by TicketKeyGeneratorConcurrencyTest.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sprintId": 1,
  "title": "Write more .http requests",
  "description": "Self-referential, but someone has to do it."
}

> {%
    client.global.set("ticketId", response.body.id);
%}

### EXERCISE A - GET ticket detail with resolved assignee name
# Run this one to check exercise A: it hits TicketController#getById, which calls
# GetTicketDetailUseCase -> TicketRepositoryAdapter.findDetailById. 501 until implemented,
# then watch for LazyInitializationException if the fix is wrong before it is green.
# Ticket 1 is seeded (KATA-SEED-1, assigned to alice) - replace the id if yours differs.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/1

### EXERCISE C demo - ticket with comments AND tags loaded together (501 until implemented)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/1/full

### EXERCISE B demo - list tickets of a sprint without N+1 queries (501 until implemented)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?sprintId=1

### Add a comment to a ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/1/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "authorId": 1,
  "body": "Looks good to me."
}

### Add a tag to a ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/1/tags
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "needs-review"
}

### Assign a ticket to a user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/1/assign
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1
}

### Move a ticket to another sprint
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/1/move
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sprintId": 2
}
